{"title": "Sectional Mock #90 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>A train crosses a pole in 30 seconds and a platform in 50 seconds. If the length of the platform is 300m, then find the speed of the train (in km/hr). </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2306;&#2349;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; 30 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335;&#2347;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 50 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335;&#2347;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 300 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; (&#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["36 km/h", "18 km/h", "72 km/h", "54 km/h"], "options_hi": ["36 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "18 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "72 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "54 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>[To convert m/sec into km/h multiply by 18/5]</p><p>Let the length of the train be 'x' m and the speed of the train be 's' m/s. </p><p>According to the question: </p><p>x = 30s ......... (1)</p><p>(x + 300) = 50s ....... (2)</p><p>Divide (1) by (2) </p><p>x/ (x + 300) = 30s/50s = 3/5</p><p>5x = 3x + 900</p><p>x = 450</p><p>From equation (1): </p><p>450 = 30s</p><p>s = 15 m/s</p><p>s = 15 * (18/5)</p><p>s = 54 km/h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>[To convert m/sec into km/h multiply by 18/5]</p><p>Let the length of the train be 'x' m and the speed of the train be 's' m/s. </p><p>According to the question: </p><p>x = 30s ......... (1)</p><p>(x + 300) = 50s ....... (2)</p><p>Divide (1) by (2) </p><p>x/ (x + 300) = 30s/50s = 3/5</p><p>5x = 3x + 900</p><p>x = 450</p><p>From equation (1): </p><p>450 = 30s</p><p>s = 15 m/s</p><p>s = 15 * (18/5)</p><p>s = 54 km/h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If a + b is an even number, then which of the following can be true?</p><p>I: Both a and b are even numbers</p><p>II: a is an even number and b is an odd number</p><p>III: Both a and b are odd numbers</p>", "q_hi": "<p>1 &#2360;&#2375; 20 &#2340;&#2325; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376; - </p>", "options_en": ["Only I", "Both II and III", "Only II", "Both I and III"], "options_hi": ["102", "112", "115", "108"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Sum of prime numbers between 30 and 40 = 31 + 37 = 68</p><p>Sum of prime number between 40 and 50 = 41 + 43 + 47 = 131</p><p>Difference = 131  -  68 = 63</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Sum of prime numbers between 30 and 40 = 31 + 37 = 68</p><p>Sum of prime number between 40 and 50 = 41 + 43 + 47 = 131</p><p>Difference = 131  -  68 = 63</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Study the following data and choose the INCORRECT option.</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Animals</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Population percentage</b></td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Lions</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">12%</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Crocodiles</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">28%</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Rabbits</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">27%</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Monkeys</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">33%</td></tr></table>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2305;&#2325;&#2396;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; <b>&#2327;&#2354;&#2340;</b> &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2332;&#2368;&#2357;-&#2332;&#2306;&#2340;&#2369;</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2332;&#2344;&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340;</b></td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2358;&#2375;&#2352;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">12%</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2350;&#2327;&#2352;&#2350;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">28%</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2326;&#2352;&#2327;&#2379;&#2358;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">27%</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2348;&#2306;&#2342;&#2352;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">33%</td></tr></table>", "options_en": ["If total animals are 6200, then number of lions are 744", "If total animals are 7000, then number of Crocodiles are 1960", "If total animals are 4500, then number of Rabbits are 1210", "If total animals are 3400, then number of Monkeys are 1122"], "options_hi": ["&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;-&#2332;&#2306;&#2340;&#2369; 6200 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2375;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 744 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;", "&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;-&#2332;&#2306;&#2340;&#2369; 7000 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2327;&#2352;&#2350;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 1960 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;", "&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;-&#2332;&#2306;&#2340;&#2369; 4500 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2326;&#2352;&#2327;&#2379;&#2358;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 1210 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;", "&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;-&#2332;&#2306;&#2340;&#2369; 3400 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2306;&#2342;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 1122 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>According to the question,</p><p>Option (a)</p><p>Total animals = 6200</p><p>Population percentage of lions =12%</p><p>Number of lions= 12% of total population</p><p>=12% x 6200</p><p>= 744</p><p>(CORRECT)</p><p>Option (b)</p><p>Total animals = 7000</p><p>Population percentage of crocodiles =28%</p><p>Number of crocodiles= 28% of total population</p><p>=28% x 7000</p><p>=1960</p><p>(CORRECT)</p><p>Option (c)</p><p>Total animals = 4500</p><p>Population percentage of rabbits =27%</p><p>Number of rabbits= 27% of total population</p><p>= 27% x 4500</p><p>=1215</p><p>(INCORRECT)</p><p>Option (d)</p><p>Total animals = 3400</p><p>Population percentage of Monkeys =33%</p><p>Number of monkeys = 33% of total population</p><p>=33% x 3400</p><p>=1122</p><p>(CORRECT)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the question,</p><p>Option (a)</p><p>Total animals = 6200</p><p>Population percentage of lions =12%</p><p>Number of lions= 12% of total population</p><p>=12% x 6200</p><p>= 744</p><p>(CORRECT)</p><p>Option (b)</p><p>Total animals = 7000</p><p>Population percentage of crocodiles =28%</p><p>Number of crocodiles= 28% of total population</p><p>=28% x 7000</p><p>=1960</p><p>(CORRECT)</p><p>Option (c)</p><p>Total animals = 4500</p><p>Population percentage of rabbits =27%</p><p>Number of rabbits= 27% of total population</p><p>= 27% x 4500</p><p>=1215</p><p>(INCORRECT)</p><p>Option (d)</p><p>Total animals = 3400</p><p>Population percentage of Monkeys =33%</p><p>Number of monkeys = 33% of total population</p><p>=33% x 3400</p><p>=1122</p><p>(CORRECT)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If (a<sup>3</sup>+b<sup>3</sup>+c<sup>3</sup>-3abc) = 330, and (a+b+c) = 11, find the value of (a-b)<sup>2</sup>+(b-c)<sup>2</sup>+(c-a)<sup>2</sup>.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; (a<sup>3</sup>+b<sup>3</sup>+c<sup>3</sup>-3abc) = 330, &#2324;&#2352; (a+b+c) = 11, &#2340;&#2379; (a-b)<sup>2</sup>+(b-c)<sup>2</sup>+(c-a)<sup>2</sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["52", "60", "50", "55"], "options_hi": ["52", "60", "50", "55"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>(a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + c<sup>3</sup> - 3abc) = 1/2 (a + b + c) [(a - b)<sup>2</sup> + (b - c)<sup>2</sup>+(c - a)<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>=&gt; 330 = 1/2  X  11 (a - b)<sup>2</sup> + (b - c)<sup>2</sup>+(c - a)<sup>2</sup>.</p><p>=&gt; (a - b)<sup>2</sup> + (b - c)<sup>2</sup>+(c - a)<sup>2</sup> = 660/11</p><p>=&gt; (a - b)<sup>2</sup> + (b - c)<sup>2</sup>+(c - a)<sup>2</sup> = 60</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>(a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + c<sup>3</sup> - 3abc) = 1/2 (a + b + c) [(a - b)<sup>2</sup> + (b - c)<sup>2</sup>+(c - a)<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>=&gt; 330 = 1/2  X  11 (a - b)<sup>2</sup> + (b - c)<sup>2</sup>+(c - a)<sup>2</sup>.</p><p>=&gt; (a - b)<sup>2</sup> + (b - c)<sup>2</sup>+(c - a)<sup>2</sup> = 660/11</p><p>=&gt; (a - b)<sup>2</sup> + (b - c)<sup>2</sup>+(c - a)<sup>2</sup> = 60</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the difference between the two numbers is 9 and the sum of their squares is 585, then find the product of the two numbers.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 9 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 585 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["264", "252", "248", "260"], "options_hi": ["264", "252", "248", "260"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>a  -  b = 9, a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> = 585</p><p>(a  -  b)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>  -  2ab</p><p>9<sup>2</sup> = 585  -  2ab </p><p>ab = (585  -  81)/2 = 252</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>a  -  b = 9, a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> = 585</p><p>(a  -  b)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>  -  2ab</p><p>9<sup>2</sup> = 585  -  2ab </p><p>ab = (585  -  81)/2 = 252</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p><span>Ram, Rahim and Raghu invest in a partnership in the ratio of 5/2,4/3, and 6/5 respectively. After 3 months, Ram increased his share by 40%. If total profit at the end of one year be Rs. 6,94,000. What is Rahim&rsquo;s share of profits?", "q_hi": "<p>&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;, &#2352;&#2361;&#2368;&#2350; &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2328;&#2369; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;: 5/2,4/3 &#2324;&#2352; 6/5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; 3 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, &#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 40% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; 6,94,000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.1,80,000", "Rs.1,60,000", "Rs. 2,00,000", "Rs. 2,50,000"], "options_hi": ["1,80,000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "1,60,000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "2,00,000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "2,50,000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the amounts invested by Ram, Rahim and Raghu be 75x, 40x and 36x respectively.</p><p>Profits are determined by= amount invested x time period</p><p>Ram : (75x x 3) + ( 75x x 140/100 x 9)=1170 x</p><p>Rahim: 40x&nbsp; x 12=480x</p><p>Raghu : 36x x 12= 432x</p><p>Ratio= 390:160:144</p><p>Rahim&rsquo;s share of profits = 694000/694 x 160= Rs. 1,60,000. Hence, option b.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the amounts invested by Ram, Rahim and Raghu be 75x, 40x and 36x respectively.</p><p>Profits are determined by= amount invested x time period</p><p>Ram : (75x x 3) + ( 75x x 140/100 x 9)=1170 x</p><p>Rahim: 40x&nbsp; x 12=480x</p><p>Raghu : 36x x 12= 432x</p><p>Ratio= 390:160:144</p><p>Rahim&rsquo;s share of profits = 694000/694 x 160= Rs. 1,60,000. Hence, option b.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>A sum is lent for 4 years at A% per annum simple interest. If the sum is lent at (A + 1.5)%, then it earns Rs.120 more. Find the sum.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 4 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; A% &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; (A + 1.5)% &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 120 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.2400", "Rs.2000", "Rs.2100", "Rs.2500"], "options_hi": ["2400 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "2000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "2100 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "2500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the sum be Rs. P.</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>P * (A + 1.5  -  A) * 4 = 120 * 100</p><p>P * 6 = 12000</p><p>P = Rs.2000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the sum be Rs. P.</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>P * (A + 1.5  -  A) * 4 = 120 * 100</p><p>P * 6 = 12000</p><p>P = Rs.2000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>Ratio of present age of A to B is 3:5 and after 6 years the ratio becomes 21:31. Find the age of B before 3 years. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; B &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 3:5 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 6 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2351;&#2361; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 21:31 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["20 years", "23 years", "22 years", "24 years"], "options_hi": ["20 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "23 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "22 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "24 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the present age of A and B be 3x years and 5x years respectively.</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(3x + 6)/(5x + 6) = 21/31</p><p>93x + 186 = 105x + 126</p><p>x = 5 </p><p>Present age of B = 5 * 5 = 25 years</p><p>Age of B before 3 years = 25  -  3 = 22 years</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the present age of A and B be 3x years and 5x years respectively.</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(3x + 6)/(5x + 6) = 21/31</p><p>93x + 186 = 105x + 126</p><p>x = 5 </p><p>Present age of B = 5 * 5 = 25 years</p><p>Age of B before 3 years = 25  -  3 = 22 years</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>The base radius and height of a cylinder are 12 cm and 35 cm respectively. Find the curved surface area (in cm<sup>2</sup> of cylinder.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 12 cm &#2324;&#2352; 35 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (cm<sup>2</sup> &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["2420", "2640", "2810", "2220"], "options_hi": ["2420", "2640", "2810", "2220"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Curved surface area of cylinder = 2 * &pi; * r * h</p><p>= 2 * (22/7) * 12 * 35</p><p>= 44 * 60</p><p>= 2640 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Curved surface area of cylinder = 2 * &pi; * r * h</p><p>= 2 * (22/7) * 12 * 35</p><p>= 44 * 60</p><p>= 2640 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The given table shows the number of books available on different stores.</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Stores</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Number of Books</b></td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>S1</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">240</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>S2</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">380</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>S3</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">290</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>S4</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">340</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>S5</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">420</td></tr></table><p>What is the ratio of the number of books in store S1 to the average of total number of books from all stores together?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2340;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2346;&#2354;&#2348;&#2381;&#2343; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2379;&#2352;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">S1</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">240</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">S2</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">380</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">S3</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">290</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">S4</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">340</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">S5</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">420</td></tr></table><p>&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2379;&#2352; S1 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2379;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["97 : 123", "85 : 97", "120 : 167", "125 : 167"], "options_hi": ["97 : 123", "85 : 97", "120 : 167", "125 : 167"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Number of books in store S1 = 240</p><p>Average of total number of books from all stores together = (240 + 380 + 290 + 340 + 420)/5</p><p>=&gt; 1670/5 = 334</p><p>Required ratio = 240 : 334 = 120 : 167</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of books in store S1 = 240</p><p>Average of total number of books from all stores together = (240 + 380 + 290 + 340 + 420)/5</p><p>=&gt; 1670/5 = 334</p><p>Required ratio = 240 : 334 = 120 : 167</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of two numbers is 2 : 5 and their difference is 210. The smaller number is __________.</p>", "q_hi": "&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 2 : 5 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 210 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; __________ &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;", "options_en": ["60", "130", "140", "350"], "options_hi": ["60", "130", "140", "350"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the two numbers be 2x and 5x respectively,</p><p>According to question, </p><p>5x  -  2x = 210</p><p>3x = 210</p><p>x = 70</p><p>smaller number = 2x = 140</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the two numbers be 2x and 5x respectively,</p><p>According to question, </p><p>5x  -  2x = 210</p><p>3x = 210</p><p>x = 70</p><p>smaller number = 2x = 140</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>A boat covers 110 km in upstream and 196 km in downstream in 12 hours. If it covers 375 km in still water in 15 hours, then what is the speed of the stream?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; 12 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 110 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 196 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2351;&#2361; 15 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 375 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["4 km/h", "3 km/h", "2 km/h", "5 km/h"], "options_hi": ["4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "3 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "2 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "5 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let speed of stream = 'v' km/h</p><p>Speed of boat in still water = 375/15 = 25 km/h</p><p>Now,</p><p>110/(25 - v) + 196/(25 + v) = 12</p><p>v = 3 km/h</p><p>So, speed of stream = 3 km/h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let speed of stream = 'v' km/h</p><p>Speed of boat in still water = 375/15 = 25 km/h</p><p>Now,</p><p>110/(25 - v) + 196/(25 + v) = 12</p><p>v = 3 km/h</p><p>So, speed of stream = 3 km/h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the area of the base of a regular hexagonal pyramid is 216&radic;3 m<sup>2</sup> and the area of one of its faces is 72&radic;3 m2, then find the volume of the pyramid.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2359;&#2335;&#2381;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339;&#2368;&#2351; &#2346;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2337; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 216&radic;3 m<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 72&radic;3 m2 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["646&radic;3 m3", "864&radic;3 m<sup>3</sup>", "2592&radic;3 m<sup>3</sup>", "1296&radic;3 m<sup>3</sup>"], "options_hi": ["646&radic;3 &#2319;&#2350;3", "864&radic;3 &#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "2592&radic;3 &#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "1296&radic;3 &#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Area of base of hexagonal pyramid = 3&radic;3/2 * base<sup>2</sup></p><p>216&radic;3 = 3&radic;3/2 * base<sup>2</sup></p><p>base<sup>2</sup> = 144 m<sup>2</sup></p><p>base = 12 m</p><p>Area of one face = 1/2 * base * slant height </p><p>72&radic;3 = 1/2 * 12 * slant height </p><p>Slant height = 12&radic;3 m</p><p>Height = &radic;[(12&radic;3)<sup>2</sup>  -  (12&radic;3/2)<sup>2</sup>] = 18 m</p><p>The volume of the pyramid = 1/3 * area of hexagon * Height of the pyramid</p><p>= 1/3 * 216&radic;3 * 18</p><p>= 1296&radic;3 m<sup>3</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Area of base of hexagonal pyramid = 3&radic;3/2 * base<sup>2</sup></p><p>216&radic;3 = 3&radic;3/2 * base<sup>2</sup></p><p>base<sup>2</sup> = 144 m<sup>2</sup></p><p>base = 12 m</p><p>Area of one face = 1/2 * base * slant height </p><p>72&radic;3 = 1/2 * 12 * slant height </p><p>Slant height = 12&radic;3 m</p><p>Height = &radic;[(12&radic;3)<sup>2</sup>  -  (12&radic;3/2)<sup>2</sup>] = 18 m</p><p>The volume of the pyramid = 1/3 * area of hexagon * Height of the pyramid</p><p>= 1/3 * 216&radic;3 * 18</p><p>= 1296&radic;3 m<sup>3</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A loan of Rs. 7800 is to be paid back in two equal half-yearly installments. How much is each installment if the interest is compounded half-yearly at 16 % per annum? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>7800 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2319; &#2325;&#2366; &#2315;&#2339; &#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;-&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; 16% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;-&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 4395", "Rs. 4280", "Rs. 4275", "Rs. 4374"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 4395", "&#2352;&#2369;. 4280", "&#2352;&#2369;. 4275", "&#2352;&#2369;. 4374"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>[In half yearly, time doubles and interest half]</p><p>16%/2 = 8% </p><p>Let the instalment be Rs. 'X'</p><p>[P * (1 + R/100)  -  X] * (1 + R/100) = X </p><p>[7800 * (1 + 8/100)  -  X] * (1 + 8/100) = X </p><p>[7800 * 108/100  -  X] * 108/100 = X </p><p>7800 * 27/25  -  X = X * 25/27 </p><p>7800 * 27/25 = 25X/27 + X </p><p>52X/27 = 7800 * 27/25 </p><p>X = Rs. 4374 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>[In half yearly, time doubles and interest half]</p><p>16%/2 = 8% </p><p>Let the instalment be Rs. 'X'</p><p>[P * (1 + R/100)  -  X] * (1 + R/100) = X </p><p>[7800 * (1 + 8/100)  -  X] * (1 + 8/100) = X </p><p>[7800 * 108/100  -  X] * 108/100 = X </p><p>7800 * 27/25  -  X = X * 25/27 </p><p>7800 * 27/25 = 25X/27 + X </p><p>52X/27 = 7800 * 27/25 </p><p>X = Rs. 4374 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>A bucket in the shape of frustrum of a cone has the top radius of 20cm and the bottom radius is 14cm. Height of the bucket is 70cm. Calculate the volume of water that can be stored in the bucket:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2331;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2366;&#2354;&#2381;&#2335;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2330;&#2354;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2366;&#2354;&#2381;&#2335;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 70 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2366;&#2354;&#2381;&#2335;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2350;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2339;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;:</p>", "options_en": ["68.24 litres", "62.24 litres", "64.24 litres", "66.24 litres"], "options_hi": ["68.24 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "62.24 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "64.24 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "66.24 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=305 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20728/image011.png\"></p><p><img width=345 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20728/image012.png\"></p><p>1 cm<sup>3</sup> = 1 ml</p><p>Therefore, 64240 cm<sup>3</sup> = 64240 ml = 64.24 litres</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=305 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20728/image011.png\"></p><p><img width=345 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20728/image012.png\"></p><p>1 cm<sup>3</sup> = 1 ml</p><p>Therefore, 64240 cm<sup>3</sup> = 64240 ml = 64.24 litres</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Number of digits in the square root of 42627841 is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>42627841 &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["5", "4", "3", "8"], "options_hi": ["5", "4", "3", "8"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>The total number of digits in 42627841 = 8</p><p>Hence required number of digits in the square root = 8/2 = 4</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The total number of digits in 42627841 = 8</p><p>Hence required number of digits in the square root = 8/2 = 4</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>If A, B and C invested Rs 2000, Rs 3000 and Rs 4000 for 8 months, 6 months and 4 months respectively, then they will share the profit in what ratio?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 8 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375;, 6 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 4 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2352;&#2369;.2000, &#2352;&#2369;.3000 &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2369;.4000 &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2375; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["9:8:10", "10:8:8", "8:9:7", "8:9:8"], "options_hi": ["9:8:10", "10:8:8", "8:9:7", "8:9:8"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Ratio in which the profit will be shared</p><p>= (2000*8) : (3000*6) : (4000*4)</p><p>= 16000 : 18000 : 16000</p><p>= 8 : 9 : 8</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Ratio in which the profit will be shared</p><p>= (2000*8) : (3000*6) : (4000*4)</p><p>= 16000 : 18000 : 16000</p><p>= 8 : 9 : 8</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>If X<sup>2</sup> = 202  -  Y<sup>2</sup>, and X = 2 + Y, then find the value of XY.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; X<sup>2</sup> = 202 - Y<sup>2 </sup>&#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; X = 2 + Y &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; XY &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["99", "120", "63", "80"], "options_hi": ["99", "120", "63", "80"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>X<sup>2</sup> = 202  -  Y<sup>2</sup></p><p>X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> = 202... (1)</p><p>X = 2 + Y</p><p>X  -  Y = 2</p><p>Square both sides,</p><p>X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> - 2XY = 4</p><p>202  -  2XY = 4</p><p>198 = 2XY</p><p>XY = 99</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>X<sup>2</sup> = 202  -  Y<sup>2</sup></p><p>X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> = 202... (1)</p><p>X = 2 + Y</p><p>X  -  Y = 2</p><p>Square both sides,</p><p>X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> - 2XY = 4</p><p>202  -  2XY = 4</p><p>198 = 2XY</p><p>XY = 99</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Nishu lends (17/24)<sup>th </sup>part of Rs.12000 to Arun at 12% rate of simple interest for 2 years and rest of the amount to Sanam at 9% rate of simple interest for 2 years. Find the difference between the total amount that Nishu gets from Arun and that from Sanam after 2 years.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2369;, &#2309;&#2352;&#2369;&#2339; &#2325;&#2379; 12000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; (17/24)<sup>&#2357;&#2366;&#2306;</sup> &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; 2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 12% &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2360;&#2344;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 9% &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; &#2309;&#2352;&#2369;&#2339; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2344;&#2350; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.6410", "Rs.6140", "Rs.6400", "Rs.6440"], "options_hi": ["6410 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "6140 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "6400 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "6440 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Total amount Nishu lends = Rs.12000</p><p>Amount Nishu lends to Arun = 12000* 17/24 = Rs.8500</p><p>Amount Nishu lends to Sanam = 12000  -  8500 = Rs.3500</p><p>Total amount Nishu gets from Arun after 2 years = 8500 + (8500* 12* 2)/100</p><p>= 8500 + 2040 = Rs.10540</p><p>Total amount Nishu gets from Sanam after 2 years = 3500 + (3500* 9* 2)/100</p><p>= 3500 + 630 = Rs.4130</p><p>Required difference = 10540  -  4130 = Rs.6410</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total amount Nishu lends = Rs.12000</p><p>Amount Nishu lends to Arun = 12000* 17/24 = Rs.8500</p><p>Amount Nishu lends to Sanam = 12000  -  8500 = Rs.3500</p><p>Total amount Nishu gets from Arun after 2 years = 8500 + (8500* 12* 2)/100</p><p>= 8500 + 2040 = Rs.10540</p><p>Total amount Nishu gets from Sanam after 2 years = 3500 + (3500* 9* 2)/100</p><p>= 3500 + 630 = Rs.4130</p><p>Required difference = 10540  -  4130 = Rs.6410</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>A cone is put inside a cylinder in such a way that the volume of cone is 1/8 of the volume of cylinder. If base area of cone and cylinder are equal and height of cylinder is 24 cm, find the height of cone.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2342;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2352;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344;, &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; 1/8 &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 24 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["8 cm", "10 cm", "9 cm", "7 cm"], "options_hi": ["8 cm", "10 cm", "9 cm", "7 cm"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of cone = 1/8 * volume of cylinder</p><p>1/3 * &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h = 1/8 * &#960;r<sup>2</sup> * 24</p><p>Height of cone = 9 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of cone = 1/8 * volume of cylinder</p><p>1/3 * &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h = 1/8 * &#960;r<sup>2</sup> * 24</p><p>Height of cone = 9 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A 6-digit number, 24567X is divisible by 3. Find the least value of X.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; 6-&#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 24567X, 3 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1", "2", "0", "3"], "options_hi": ["1", "2", "0", "3"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Sum of digits of 24567X = 24 + X</p><p>To be divisible by 3, the least value of X = 0</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Sum of digits of 24567X = 24 + X</p><p>To be divisible by 3, the least value of X = 0</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A motor car does a journey in 39 hrs, the first half at 30 km/hr and the second half at 35 km/hr. Find the distance.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2379;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; 39 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2375; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379; 30 km/hr &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2375; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379; 35 km/hr &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1370 Km", "1180 Km", "1260 Km", "1155 Km"], "options_hi": ["1370 Km", "1180 Km", "1260 Km", "1155 Km"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the distance = X km</p><p>Then X/2 km is travelled at a speed of 30 km/hr and X/2 km at a speed of 35 km/hr.</p><p>Then time taken to travel the whole journey = [X/(2*30)] + [X/(2*35)] = 39 hrs</p><p>(X/60) + (X/70) = 39</p><p>13X/420 = 39</p><p>X = 39*420/13 = 1260 Km</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the distance = X km</p><p>Then X/2 km is travelled at a speed of 30 km/hr and X/2 km at a speed of 35 km/hr.</p><p>Then time taken to travel the whole journey = [X/(2*30)] + [X/(2*35)] = 39 hrs</p><p>(X/60) + (X/70) = 39</p><p>13X/420 = 39</p><p>X = 39*420/13 = 1260 Km</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>In what ratio must a grocer mix two types of sugar costing Rs. 18/kg and Rs. 25/kg, so that the resultant mixture costs Rs. 21/kg?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2306;&#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2352;&#2369;.18/kg &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2369;.25/kg &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350;&#2368; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2352;&#2369;.21/kg &#2361;&#2379;?</p>", "options_en": ["1 : 3", "2 : 1", "4 : 3", "3 : 2"], "options_hi": ["1 : 3", "2 : 1", "4 : 3", "3 : 2"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=290 height=232 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25022/image002.gif\"></p><p>Required ratio = 4 : 3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=290 height=232 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25022/image002.gif\"></p><p>Required ratio = 4 : 3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>If p<sup>2</sup>/q<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup>/p<sup>2</sup> = 254, then find p/q + q/p?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; p<sup>2</sup>/q<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup>/p<sup>2</sup> = 254, &#2340;&#2379; p/q + q/p &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["16", "&#177;16", "-16", "32"], "options_hi": ["16", "&#177;16", "-16", "32"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>p<sup>2</sup>/q<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup>/p<sup>2</sup> = 254</p><p>p<sup>2</sup>/q<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup>/p<sup>2</sup> + 2 = 254 + 2</p><p>(p/q)<sup>2</sup> + (q/p)<sup>2</sup> + 2*(p/q)(q/p) = 256</p><p>(p/q + q/p)<sup>2</sup> = 16<sup>2</sup></p><p>p/q + q/p = &#177;16</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>p<sup>2</sup>/q<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup>/p<sup>2</sup> = 254</p><p>p<sup>2</sup>/q<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup>/p<sup>2</sup> + 2 = 254 + 2</p><p>(p/q)<sup>2</sup> + (q/p)<sup>2</sup> + 2*(p/q)(q/p) = 256</p><p>(p/q + q/p)<sup>2</sup> = 16<sup>2</sup></p><p>p/q + q/p = &#177;16</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A, B and C started a business such that amount invested by A and B are 32% and 24% respectively of total investment. B works for an year. A work for 4 more months than C and C left after 6 months. At the end of one-year partnership, profit earned by them is Rs.3270. What is the share of C in profit?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 32% &#2324;&#2352; 24% &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; B &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; A, C &#2360;&#2375; 4 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; C 6 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2352;&#2369;. 3270 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2361; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; C &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.1320", "Rs.1100", "Rs.880", "Rs.990"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;.1320", "&#2352;&#2369;.1100", "&#2352;&#2369;.880", "&#2352;&#2369;.990"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let total investment = a</p><p>A's investment = 32% of a = 0.32a</p><p>B's investment = 24% of a = 0.24a</p><p>C's investment = a  -  0.32a  -  0.24a = 0.44a</p><p>C's period of investment = 6 months</p><p>A's period of investment = 4 + 6 = 10 months</p><p>B's period of investment = 12 months</p><p>Now, profit ratio: A: B: C = (0.32a * 10): (0.24a * 12): (0.44a * 6)</p><p>= 40: 36: 33</p><p>Total profit = 3270</p><p>Therefore, share of C in profit</p><p>= 3270 * 33/(40 + 36 + 33)</p><p>= <b>Rs.990</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let total investment = a</p><p>A's investment = 32% of a = 0.32a</p><p>B's investment = 24% of a = 0.24a</p><p>C's investment = a  -  0.32a  -  0.24a = 0.44a</p><p>C's period of investment = 6 months</p><p>A's period of investment = 4 + 6 = 10 months</p><p>B's period of investment = 12 months</p><p>Now, profit ratio: A: B: C = (0.32a * 10): (0.24a * 12): (0.44a * 6)</p><p>= 40: 36: 33</p><p>Total profit = 3270</p><p>Therefore, share of C in profit</p><p>= 3270 * 33/(40 + 36 + 33)</p><p>= <b>Rs.990</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}]}